; open-questions-band.fk — two or three live at all times, and a hand that can reach them.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/open-questions.fk
;
; The invariant is Urs's, stated 2026-07-23 00:52. The gesture channel is measured: of
; three candidate sensors polled four times over twenty seconds, only auto_brightness was
; live — proximity frozen three days, light CCT frozen an hour.
;
; Verdict 255 when, on Go / Rust / TypeScript / fkwu:
;     1  three questions are open right now
;     2  which is inside the two-to-three range he asked for
;     4  a queue of one fails the range — fewer, and he is being led
;     8  a queue of four fails it too — more, and he is being interrogated
;    16  every open question names what would answer it
;    32  all three open questions are offerable
;    64  a choice no hand can reach is not offerable, however good the choice
;   128  and the channel is auto_brightness, named so it can be re-witnessed later
;
; The teaching in bit 4 and bit 8: a preference stated once at midnight does not survive the
; session that heard it unless it becomes a number something checks. "Keep two or three open"
; is a mood until a band fails at one and at four.
;
; And bit 64 is sensing-playbook.fk's rule arriving from the interface side: an option a hand
; cannot reach is not on the interface. There it was a blocked recipe never offered; here it
; is a choice with no gesture assigned. Same discipline, different door.

(do
    (open-questions-check))
